        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rex Salas, Cher\n- Roles: record producer, songwriter, musical director, music arranger, singer, actress\n- Topics: music careers, artist collaborations\n\nFacts:\n- Cher was born as Cherilyn Sarkisian on May 20, 1946, and she is an American singer and actress.\n- Rex Salas was born on March 16, 1962, and he is an American record producer, songwriter, musical director, and music arranger.\n- Cher is sometimes referred to as the Goddess of Pop and has been described as embodying female autonomy in a male-dominated industry.\n- In recent years, Rex Salas has been best known for serving as Janet Jackson's musical director on several of her tours.\n- Rex Salas has worked with many artists, including Vanessa Williams, Justin Timberlake, Cher, Boyz II Men, Robert Palmer, Mariah Carey, Stevie Wonder, Lionel Richie, Earth, Wind and Fire, will.i.am, Robin Thicke, 50 Cent, Jessica Simpson, Nicole Scherzinger, Adam Levine, Brandy, Maxwell, Leona Lewis, Brian McKnight, Teddy Pendergrass, The Isley Brothers, The Jacksons, Gladys Knight, Patti Austin, Sheena Easton, and Level 42.",
